  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 1,
              "start": 1
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners were represented by Kenneth S. Geller, and the United States filed an amicus brief supporting them."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 1,
              "start": 1
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent, John Garamendi, was represented by Frank Kaplan."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the California statute would interfere with U.S. foreign\u2011policy goals and the ICHEIC system, which two Presidents have said serves the best interests of Holocaust victims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States (amicus) contends that the statute is not a general law but targets foreign insurance transactions from more than 50 years ago, a matter traditionally handled by the national government."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States argues that disclosure is a form of regulation that falls under federal securities law, so a state may not enforce its policies on disclosure of information in other states."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States claims the statute violates the Constitution because it impedes longstanding national efforts to cooperate with European countries on Holocaust claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States warns that the impact of the statute would be felt by the nation as a whole, affecting U.S. relations with European countries."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "California",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to California, california asserts an interest in obtaining information that companies doing business in the state have been unwilling to provide."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "California notes that the law is similar to a European directive on disclosure."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, justices asked whether the President can preempt state law on foreign\u2011policy grounds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice (question)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f220775f324cefee39d041dfdee1f2eeb4c1d0d65e9b33b4a3c01915950a1397",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f220775f324c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice (question), justices questioned whether a preemptive statute or treaty would invoke the Supremacy Clause rather than the President\u2019s foreign\u2011affairs power."
      }
