    "summary": "The Supreme Court heard arguments on April 23, 2003, in a dispute over a California law that would require disclosure of information about foreign\u2011insurance policies tied to Holocaust\u2011era claims. The petitioners argue the law interferes with U.S. foreign policy and the International Commission on Holocaust Era Insurance Claims (ICHEIC). The United States, filing as amicus, says the statute intrudes on a matter traditionally handled by the federal government and violates the Constitution. California says it has a legitimate interest in obtaining the information.",
